# Security headers for the frontend. Netlify serves dist/_headers after a
# `vite build` (public/* is copied into dist/). The frontend is currently
# hosted behind Cloudflare on shooter.academy; these headers take effect when
# the frontend is built and served from this repository, and the same headers
# should be mirrored on the active hosting/CDN.
#
# CSP is now ENFORCED (no longer Report-Only). Two deliberate carve-outs:
#   * script-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' until the hosting layer stops injecting
#     inline scripts into index.html (Cloudflare challenge bootstrap). Removing
#     it today would hard-break the site on the first challenge; the follow-up
#     is to serve those as external files and drop the token.
#   * bolt.new is intentionally NOT allow-listed: enforcement is what removes
#     the third-party badge script from the page.
# cloudflareinsights.com stays allow-listed so first-party analytics keeps
# working instead of failing silently.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://shooter.academy https://*.supabase.co; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://cloudflareinsights.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
